.TH MODELVIEW 1
.SH NAME
modelview \- inspect three-dimensional models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modelview
[
.B -n
.I frames
]
[
.B -o
.I screenshot.png
]
[
.I model
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Modelview
opens a model in a rio window using raygui controls and raylib's classic
OpenGL renderer. With no file it displays a generated torus.
OBJ, IQM, glTF/GLB, M3D and VOX files use raylib's existing loaders.
Associated textures are loaded relative to the model as supported by
those loaders. The view is centered and scaled to fit the model's bounds.
.PP
Drag with button 1 to orbit; the wheel zooms.
Space toggles automatic rotation and R resets the camera.
The toolbar opens another file, toggles grid, wireframe and lighting,
and sets the rotation and animation speed.
Enter accepts an edited path; Open loads the path explicitly.
An unsuccessful open preserves the current model.
An empty path restores the torus.
Escape leaves path editing or, when not editing, exits.
.PP
Models with embedded animation expose Animate and Next controls.
Keyframes are interpolated on the CPU, using 60 keyframes per second at
speed 1. The API does not expose source timing; use Speed to adjust it.
Static views wait for input instead of redrawing continuously.
.PP
.B -n
exits after the specified number of displayed frames.
.B -o
saves the final frame as a PNG, including the controls.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/modelview
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR raygui (2),
.IR raylib (2),
.IR tinygl (2),
.IR rio (4)
.SH BUGS
Requires QEMU VirGL and the native GPU driver.
Materials use classic GL; programmable shaders and physically based
material effects are unavailable. Separate animation files are not loaded.
Window targets are limited to 2048 by 2048 pixels.
